  "body": "What happens: the Mach4 post writes a whole-second dwell on `G82` or `G89` without a decimal point. A 1 s dwell posts `P1`. Mach4 can read a P word with no decimal point as milliseconds, so the dwell can be 1000 times too short.\n\nExpected: the post writes the dwell so that it has one meaning on every Mach4 setting (for example `P1.`), or it writes milliseconds as a whole number on purpose.\n\nEvidence (upstream/main `f0bdc5109`):\n- `assets/posts/mach4.cps:841` writes `\"P\" + trimDec(secDwell, 3, false)`. `trimDec` (lines 92-99) removes the decimal point of a whole number.\n- The only test, `mach4_post.rs` (lines 266-285), pins `P0.25`. No test pins a whole-second dwell.\n\nFound by the post audit against the Mach4 manuals (#4130).\n\nDone means: a 1 s and a 2 s dwell post with a decimal point (or as documented milliseconds), and a test pins each.\n",
